<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-10047] MVCC: Wrong coordinator assignment when two oldest nodes fail.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-10047</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Reproducer: &lt;tt&gt;CacheContinuousQueryFailoverMvccTxSelfTest#testLeftPrimaryAndBackupNodes&lt;/tt&gt;. This test can sporadically hangs when topology is unstable.&lt;br/&gt;
The problem here is when two oldest nodes A and B failed, other nodes elect B node as a new coordinator despite it is down. This happens because the new mvcc coordinator is assigned in  &lt;tt&gt;GridDhtPartitionsExchangeFuture#init&lt;/tt&gt; method which is called only ones in case of multiple nodes fail simultaneously. &lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13194856">IGNITE-10047</key>
